POINT 1: FACE DATA\
\
Apple's Note:\
\
"We need additional information about how the app uses face data. Please provide answers to 6 questions about the collection, use, storage, and sharing of face data."\
\
What we did:\
\
Updated Privacy Policy in the app (Section 7 "Face ID (Face Recognition)") and in the app.\
\
Answers to all 6 Apple questions:\
\
1. What face data does the app collect?\
\
The app does NOT collect face data. We only use Face ID \'97 a built-in iOS function for local authentication. Face data is processed exclusively by the iOS operating system in the device's Secure Enclave. We do not have access to the user's face data.\
\
2. How is this data used?\
\
Face ID is used only for user authentication when logging into the app. Face data is not used for any other purposes. Processing occurs locally on the device without data transmission.\
\
3. Is it shared with third parties? Where is it stored?\
\
No, face data is NOT shared with third parties. Data is stored only locally on the device in Secure Enclave \'97 a protected area of the processor to which we do not have access. Data is not transmitted to our servers or third parties.\
\
4. How long is it retained?\
\
Face data is stored only on the device until:\
- The user deletes the app\
- The user disables Face ID in device settings\
- The user resets device settings\
\
We do not store face data on our servers.\
\
5. Where in the Privacy Policy is this described?\
\
Section "Registration and authentication" in the app's Privacy Policy, points 4-6. Also available on the website: https://aladdin-ai.ru/privacy.html (Section 7 "Face ID (Face Recognition)").\
\
6. Quote the specific text from the Privacy Policy:\
\
Section 7 "Face ID (Face Recognition)":\
- The app uses Face ID for secure user authentication.\
- Face data is NOT collected \'97 the app uses only the built-in iOS function for local authentication.\
- Face data is NOT shared with third parties \'97 all processing occurs locally on the device in Secure Enclave.\
- Face data is NOT stored on our servers \'97 it remains only on the user's device.\
- Face data is deleted when the app is removed or Face ID is disabled in device settings.\
- We do not have access to the user's face data \'97 it is processed exclusively by the iOS operating system.\
\
